t=Table(rows,colWidths=[124,119,78,175]);t.setStyle(TableStyle([('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,0),colors.HexColor('#e6f1f4')),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'TOP'),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),9),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),9),('LINEBELOW',(0,0),(-1,-1),.5,colors.HexColor('#d6e2e8'))]));story.extend([t,Spacer(1,10),p('The mix-shift fixture preserves segment outcome rates. Its raw decline is composition, not within-segment deterioration. A current-stage investigation priority is a different question from explaining the historical decline.'),p('Try the offline demo','H'),p('Open output/dashboard.html. Change scenario, segment and recovery assumptions; compare raw and adjusted rates, inspect exclusions, then export a cohort CSV and decision JSON. The five scenarios offer 500 precomputed views. No accounts, server or network are required.'),PageBreak(),p('Defensible before sophisticated','TitleX'),p('Measurement and engineering','H'),p('One advertiser initial planning attempt is the analytical unit. Both cohorts have the same inclusive 14-day horizon. All funnel rates use mature, complete and valid attempts; missing telemetry is an exclusion, not a failed conversion. Baseline segment weights define the same comparison population across periods.'),p('Python validates clocks and identities before SQLite derives one row per attempt. Exact retries collapse; event conflicts quarantine affected advertisers. Ambiguous advertiser dimensions abort the run rather than bias segment results by input order. Fractional-second timestamps are rejected instead of rounded across boundaries.'),p('Missing segment support, small cells or excessive incomplete/invalid coverage block the recommendation. Recovery fractions and decision thresholds are illustrative policy. Wilson bounds only illustrate raw-rate binomial precision; there is no claimed causal or adjusted-rate uncertainty interval.'),p('What improves on the prior lab','H'),p('The separate entry adds an advertiser planning/launch question, temporal cohorts, a pure-mix scenario, explicit recovery sensitivity, a break-even point, coverage holds and no-data behavior. It reuses the Content Measurement Lab\'s strengths in grain, event-time validation, SQL lineage and interpretation. The original project is preserved.'),p('Validation and remaining limits','H'),p('The review packet includes independent mathematical and engineering reviews, deterministic rebuild checks, adversarial tests and actual-browser checks of every advertised control combination and exports. Consult docs/VALIDATION.md for the final observed counts and scope.'),p('Data and methodology: advertisers and events are fictional; no employer or client data is used. This is not an ad auction, demand forecast, production ML system or completed experiment. It omits budgets, supply constraints, seasonality, repeat attempts, intervention costs and revenue. Exact fixture outcomes are designed rather than fitted. A recovered completed plan does not guarantee a launch.'),p('Before a real intervention','H'),p('Reconcile instrumentation, inspect excluded advertisers, investigate abandonment reasons, estimate costs and define a common terminal outcome. Then prospectively evaluate the intervention with a primary metric and guardrails. Adding a complex model before these steps would hide uncertainty rather than resolve it.'),p('Walkthrough','H'),p('Explain the grain, fixed reference weights, exclusion policy, mix-shift result and score-unit limitation. Demonstrate a changed recommendation and a measurement hold. Trace both exports back to the selected cohort and assumptions.'),Spacer(1,10),p('Rebuild: python -B build.py<br/>Tests: python -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v<br/>All runtime analysis uses the Python standard library. PDF generation is optional.','SmallX')])
